menu "Audio engine"
config AUDIO_ANTIALIAS_CACHE
    bool
    default y if PAJONIIIR_BOARD_M3
    default n


config AUDIO_SCRATCH_ENABLED
    bool "Enable vinyl/scratch mode (jog platter scratches the audio)"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, touching the FLX4 jog platter top while a deck plays
        scratches the audio (forward + reverse) by driving a read head over the
        per-deck PSRAM scratch capture buffer, instead of the Phase 1 platter
        hold+scrub. Releasing seeks normal forward playback to the head position.
        Additive: with this off the output path is unchanged and touching the
        platter does the Phase 1 hold/scrub. See docs/VINYL_SCRATCH_PLAN.md.

config AUDIO_PCM_TIMELINE_SCHEDULER_PROBE
    bool "Run one-shot PCM timeline scheduler probe"
    default n
    help
        Test-build-only probe. After audio initialization, run 100 forced
        low-word wrap and playhead handoff repetitions with a higher-priority
        same-core reader, then measure both unhooked publications for 100
        repetitions. The result is written as TIMELINE_SCHEDULER_PROBE in the
        service journal.
        This isolated scheduler probe must be paired with a live dual-deck
        audio smoke; it does not qualify the ae_output path by itself. Keep
        this disabled in production and release-candidate images.

endmenu
